  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Mitre obligated $903M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, from 308 awards and an average award size of $2.9M. Obligations fell 31.6% year over year. The Department of Defense accounted for the largest share of FY2026 to date obligations with $565M, followed by the Department of Transportation with $135M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $75M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the dominant market with $698M in obligations, and Engineering Services is the next largest market with $131M. Recent fiscal-year totals show obligations of $1.5B in FY21 and FY22, $1.7B in FY23 and FY24, and $1.3B in FY25, indicating FY2026 to date is below recent full-year levels. The agency and market mix shows concentration in defense and R&D work alongside obligations from transportation, health, homeland security, commerce, and other agencies.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers of Mitre in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $565M of Mitre's FY2026 to date total. The Department of Transportation obligated $135M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $75M. Other agencies with notable obligations include the Department of Homeland Security with $51.8M and the Department of Commerce with $40.2M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services account for Mitre's FY2026 obligations?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) accounted for $698M of obligations. Engineering Services accounted for $131M and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services accounted for $61.4M. Smaller markets include Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities with $8.2M and Computer Systems Design Services with $3M."
      }
    ]
  },
